{title: Morning Light}
{arrangement: V1 C V2 C}

{start_of_verse: V1}
[G]Morning light is [C]breaking [G]through,
[Em]every day I'm made [D]anew.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: C}
[C]Sing, oh sing, my [G]soul,
[Am]lift Your name up [D]high.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: V2}
[G]Evening falls [C]upon the [G]land,
[Em]still I'm resting in Your [D]hand.
{end_of_verse}
